    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** providing the clear anchor of the lineup; his 87.42 efficiency score is fueled by a massive +19% boost against George Klassen and a lethal 0.461 xwOBA. Joining him in the elite tier are our speed-first assets, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (73.07) and **Trea Turner** (71.04), both of whom benefit significantly from projected top-of-the-order usage. **Kyle Schwarber** (71.83) also presents a strong play, as the matchup against Cade Gibson provides a favorable +4% SP skill advantage and a healthy boost from his projected leadoff spot. We are leaning into these high-probability run-scoring opportunities to offset the volatility of our middle-of-the-pack starters.\n\nStrategic platoon and park adjustments have pushed **Josh Smith** and **Kazuma Okamoto** into the lineup despite lower base projections. While their raw output is marginal, the +18% SP skill bump against Nick Martinez makes them efficient starts compared to the bench. The most difficult decision rested on **Hector Rodriguez**, who hovered just outside the starting nine with a 53.36 score. While **Hector Rodriguez** showcased a positive platoon edge, the optimizer ultimately favored **Kazuma Okamoto** due to the higher projected SP skill utilization against the same opponent. \n\nOwners should monitor lineups closely, as all projections assume historical batting order positions; any drop in the order for **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** or **Junior Caminero** would immediately deflate their efficiency scores. Furthermore, while **Christian Yelich** earns a start due to his 53.26 score and a notable +13% platoon boost against Bryce Miller, the risk remains that his low SP skill interaction (-13%) keeps his floor dangerously thin. We are currently holding **Colt Keith**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Carson Benge**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Pedro Ramirez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Jacob Gonzalez** in reserve, prepared to rotate based on late-breaking weather or confirmed lineup shifts.",
